## DictionaryPopup Component

### File Location
[src/components/DictionaryPopup.vue](mdc:src/components/DictionaryPopup.vue)

### Purpose
Display dictionary entry with multi-terminal responsive design (mobile drawer / tablet tooltip / PC sidebar).

### Props

```javascript
{
  visible: {
    type: Boolean,
    required: true
  },
  termData: {
    type: Object,
    required: true
  },
  position: {
    type: Object,
    default: () => ({ x: 0, y: 0 })
  }
}
```

### Events

```javascript
@close
```

### Responsive Detection

```javascript
import { useWindowSize } from '@vueuse/core'

const { width } = useWindowSize()
const isMobile = computed(() => width.value < 768)
const isTablet = computed(() => width.value >= 768 && width.value < 1024)
const isDesktop = computed(() => width.value >= 1024)

// Popup position based on device
const popupPosition = computed(() => {
  if (isMobile.value) return 'bottom'
  if (isTablet.value) return 'bubble'
  return 'right'
})
```

### Template Structure

```vue
<template>
  <teleport to="body">
    <transition :name="transitionName">
      <van-popup
        v-if="visible"
        :position="popupPosition"
        :style="popupStyle"
        @click-overlay="$emit('close')"
      >
        <!-- Mobile: Bottom drawer -->
        <div v-if="isMobile" class="dict-popup mobile">
          <div class="popup-header">
            <h3 class="term-title">{{ termData.term }}</h3>
            <van-icon name="cross" @click="$emit('close')" />
          </div>
          <div class="popup-content">
            <!-- Content here -->
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <!-- Tablet: Bubble -->
        <div v-else-if="isTablet" class="dict-popup tablet" :style="bubbleStyle">
          <!-- Content here -->
        </div>
        
        <!-- Desktop: Sidebar -->
        <div v-else class="dict-popup desktop">
          <!-- Content here -->
        </div>
      </van-popup>
    </transition>
  </teleport>
</template>
```

### Styling

```scss
