## Common Component Patterns

### 1. Props Validation
Always validate props with `type` and `required`/`default`:
```javascript
{
  title: {
    type: String,
    required: true
  },
  count: {
    type: Number,
    default: 0
  }
}
```

### 2. Emit Naming
Use `update:modelValue` for two-way binding:
```javascript
emit('update:modelValue', newValue)
```

### 3. Computed Properties
Use computed for derived state:
```javascript
const isMobile = computed(() => width.value < 768)
```

### 4. Lifecycle Hooks
Use `onMounted` for initialization:
```javascript
onMounted(() => {
  // Initialize component
})
```

### 5. Responsive Design
Use CSS variables and mixins:
```scss
.element {
  padding: var(--space-4);
  
  @include breakpoint(mobile) {
    padding: var(--space-3);
  }
}
```

